    /* ======================================================================
       AUTHORITATIVE DESKTOP PRESENTATION SYSTEM  (single source of truth)
       ----------------------------------------------------------------------
       - Activated ONLY by html[data-layout="desktop"], set by the mode script
         from zoom-invariant signals (fine pointer + physical window width).
         It is never inferred from the CSS viewport width, so browser zoom
         cannot switch layouts.
       - Every width/height @media block above is evaluated against the fixed
         1440x900 design viewport for desktop mode (see build transform) and
         re-scoped to this attribute; the original queries remain in force for
         html:not([data-layout="desktop"]) (real tablets / phones).
       - 1440x900 stage -> uniform scale(--ds). Internal geometry is constant.
       ====================================================================== */
    html[data-layout="desktop"] {
      --app-vw: 1440px; --app-vh: 900px; --app-vw1: 14.4px; --app-vh1: 9.0px;
      --header-h: 88px; --desktop-canvas-w: 1392px; --desktop-slide-h: 812px;
      width: 100% !important; height: 100% !important;
      overflow: hidden !important;
      background: linear-gradient(#0b2a5b 0, #0b2a5b calc(var(--ds-y, 0px) + 88px * var(--ds, 1)), #eef3fb 0);
    }
    html[data-layout="desktop"] body {
      position: absolute !important; left: 0 !important; top: 0 !important;
      width: 1440px !important; height: 900px !important; max-width: none !important;
      margin: 0 !important; overflow: hidden !important;
      transform-origin: 0 0 !important;
